{"kind":"promise","text":"I will independently review the reproducible performance evidence lane at exact head 9fc6b2cf78a71733553b5b46f1005d1e2e96ff1c, and report approved or changes-requested against the named performance artifact.\n\nWHAT I UNDERSTAND THE CONDITIONS TO REQUIRE, stated now so a mismatch surfaces before the verdict rather than after it.\n\nMechanically: that the head is exactly what was pushed and the worktree clean, and that all six artifacts are live, non-stale, and resolve. I will read those off the fold rather than off the request, because a request naming an artifact is a label and only the projection says whether it stands.\n\nOn substance: whether the contract is complete across the dimensions you name — depths, checkpoint tails, projection shapes, payload sizes, concurrency, and the ten complete-operation scenarios — and whether the measurement method is honest. That second part is where I will spend most of the effort, because a performance lane that measures the wrong thing convincingly is worse than none: fixture determinism and exact reuse, fresh per-sample writable state, setup separated from measurement, alternating base and candidate sampling rather than blocked runs, what benchstat is actually being asked, whether the correctness digests are trusted rather than assumed, whether the percentiles are applicable to the sample sizes, and whether metrics that cannot be produced are stated as unavailable instead of quietly omitted.\n\nOn the workflow: bounds, permissions, secrets and retention for the manual and scheduled paths, and the Trace2 and path-privacy limits on diagnostic profiling. First-baseline honesty in particular — a lane whose first run has nothing to compare against must say so rather than present a baseline as a comparison.\n\nWHAT I WILL RUN. The focused race and real-fixture integration tests, make vet, make test, and diff-check, at the exact head, reporting measured numbers rather than that they passed. I will also try to make the measurement lie: if fixtures are meant to be reused exactly, I will check that a changed fixture is detected rather than silently re-recorded; if sampling is meant to alternate, I will check that the code does that rather than that a comment says so.\n\nHOW I WILL JUDGE. Three conclusions the discipline requires — architecture, naming the layers touched and whether their contract moves; security, examining the workflow's permissions, secrets, retention and anything a profiling path could leak; and simplification, which for a lane this size means asking what could be deleted without weakening the evidence.\n\nI will name the exact head and the primary performance artifact in the verdict, and rest it on all six artifacts, as asked.\n\nIf I find the head has moved, or an artifact is stale or retired, I will say so and stop rather than sign over ground that shifted. And if I cannot verify one of the conditions — some are about intent that code cannot settle — I will report which, rather than let silence imply I checked it."}